## GATE 1 — supervisor crash-recovery test — CLOSED ✓

TDD, as required: the test was written first and run **before** any supervisor
change — 3 of 7 cases failed (the supervisor ignored the new timing override,
so the backoff / 60s-reset / boot-timeout cases ran against the 60s production
constants and timed out). The supervisor was then changed; all 7 pass.

New test: `packages/apps/app/src/main/sidecar-server-supervisor.test.ts`.
Drives `startSidecarServer()` against a controllable fake side-car script
(deterministic crash / health behaviour) plus the **real built `dist/bin.js`**
for the parent-death case. 7/7 green:

```
✓ /health probe drives the child to ready + exposes status
✓ repeated crash → exponential-backoff restart → permanent failure
✓ 60s healthy streak resets the backoff attempt counter
✓ a ready child that exits respawns immediately — no backoff, no attempt++
✓ boot-timeout kills a child that never reports healthy
✓ stop() is graceful and idempotent
✓ parent-death: the real built side-car self-exits when stdin closes
7 passed, 0 failed
```

Coverage vs the gate's required behaviours:
- **Exponential-backoff restart** — a permanently-crashing child is restarted
  on a strictly-increasing schedule; after the schedule is exhausted (5
  retries) `onPermanentFailure` fires with `attempts: 5` and `waitForReady()`
  rejects. The test asserts the spawn count (6 = initial + 5) and that each
  inter-spawn gap is ≥ its backoff slot and strictly increasing.
- **60s healthy-streak reset** — after 2 crashes the attempt counter is 2;
  once the child has been continuously healthy for the reset window the
  counter returns to 0.
- **Ready-child immediate respawn** — a child that crashes *after* reaching
  `ready` is respawned with no backoff and no attempt increment (separate from
  the crash-during-boot path).
- **Boot-timeout** — a child that never answers `/health` is SIGKILLed after
  the boot deadline and escalates to permanent failure.
- **`/health` probe** — `ready` is reached only because `/health` answered
  200; the test also probes `/health` directly.
- **Parent-death self-exit** — spawns the real `packages/apps/server/dist/bin.js`
  with `SLAYZONE_SUPERVISED=1`, waits for its listening banner, closes the
  stdin pipe (exactly what happens when the Electron parent dies) and asserts
  the side-car self-exits within 6s. (Skips gracefully if `dist/bin.js` is not
  built.)

### Supervisor change (required to make the test fast + deterministic)

`packages/apps/app/src/main/sidecar-server-supervisor.ts` gained an **additive,
optional** `timing?: SidecarTiming` field on `SidecarServerOpts`. Every field
falls back to the existing production constant (`BACKOFF_MS`,
`HEALTHY_RESET_MS`, `HEALTH_POLL_INTERVAL_MS`, `HEALTH_BOOT_TIMEOUT_MS`,
`STOP_SIGTERM_GRACE_MS`). `main/index.ts` passes **no** `timing`, so production
behaviour is byte-identical — the override exists solely so the test can shrink
the 60s healthy-reset window and the backoff schedule. No functionality
dropped; no production behaviour changed.

### Test runner registration

`run-all.sh` (`pnpm test:unit`) now runs the supervisor test. A new
`run_test_electron_strict` runner was added because the existing
`run_test` / `run_test_no_loader` helpers pipe through `grep` and count a suite
PASS as long as *any* output is produced — a real failure would be hidden. The
strict runner uses `set -o pipefail` so a non-zero test exit propagates and
counts as FAIL. A HARD GATE test must actually gate.

